one): squeezed as GHC's"] [269 4 "// stack squeezing does, the lower thunk an indirection to this one, one frame for both (cgrun060 at"] [270 4 "// +RTS -K64k)"] [271 4 "// (the lower thunks kept blackholed in the frame's env, updated, raised or reverted with it)"] [277 5 "// in place, as pushCase"] [287 4 "// evaluated in place (newThunkN)"] [296 1 "// update overwrites a thunk with its value."] [300 31 "// the fields and the frame may live in the thunk's own allocation"] [314 1 "// apply calls f with args (eval/apply: exact, partial, over-saturated)."] [354 1 "// applyTmp is apply of arguments in a scratch buffer (App.eval's): copied wherever they outlive the call, a partial"] [355 1 "// application one object with its arguments, a partial application saturated straight into the callee's frame."] [411 1 "// ApplyV applies a value to values (a thread's start, a primop's callback)."] [421 1 "// ret handles the top frame on a return."] [424 2 "// the two frequent frames read in place (HES73): no frame copied out, its pointers cleared"] [458 4 "// a queued throwTo# delivered at the unmasking, its value the frozen control's return (GHC's)"] [471 1 "// raiseLam is the code of a thunk whose evaluation raised: entered, it raises again."] [474 1 "// RaiseFree raises its frame's first slot."] [481 1 "// raise raises a synchronous exception (raise#, raiseIO#): the stack unwound to the nearest catch"] [482 1 "// frame, the thunks under evaluation on the way updated to raise it again."] [487 1 "// raiseAsync raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread: the thunks under evaluation on"] [488 1 "// the way reverted to unevaluated (GHC freezes them; the same results)."] [493 1 "// Frozen is an evaluation an asynchronous exception interrupted (HES56 (b), GHC's raiseAsync and AP_STACK): the frames"] [494 1 "// above an update frame, their slots copied, and the control the thread was at, an expression and its slots or a return"] [495 1 "// of r and rs. The update frame's thunk takes it as its code (frozenLam): the next demand pushes the frames back and"] [496 1 "// resumes the control, so the work done is kept (an unsafePerformIO inside runs once, as GHC's)."] [505 1 "// frozenLam is a frozen thunk's code: entered, under its own update frame, it resumes the evaluation."] [526 1 "// frozenIndLam is the code of a thunk squeezed below a frozen one in its update frame: entered, it evaluates that one."] [529 1 "// EnterFree evaluates its frame's first slot."] [536 1 "// copyFramesEnv is copyFrames of fs and a copy of env, the control's slots, sharing the copy with a frame whose slots"] [537 1 "// they are."] [563 1 "// raiseAsyncFrozen raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread, a thread not running whose control is e and"] [564 1 "// env (or a return of r and rs when e is nil), as GHC's raiseAsync: each update frame above the nearest catch frame takes"] [565 1 "// the frames above it and the control as its thunk's frozen code, the next segment's control the demand of that thunk."] [566 1 "// A segment that holds a transaction's frame is not frozen: from it on, unwind's reverting."] [596 1 "// freezeThunk gives a thunk under evaluation the code l over v (raiseAsyncFrozen), unevaluated again; its waiters woken."] [631 5 "// an asynchronous exception is not catchSTM#'s: its nested writes undone, on (review 189, F9)"] [646 1 "// uncaught ends a thread whose exception reached the bottom of its stack (forkIO's and runMainIO's own"] [647 1 "// handlers catch everything, so only a thread started without them gets here: one killed before it ran,"] [648 1 "// which ends silently, as GHC's)."] [656 2 "// a thread killed before it started (forkIO's handler not yet on its stack) ends silently, as GHC's"] [659 1 "// ---- threads ----"] [669 1 "// wake makes a blocked thread runnable."] [679 1 "// block stops the current thread until it is woken; on waking it returns from the blocked call"] [680 1 "// (with the return registers its waker sets) or runs e."] [687 3 "// a queued throwTo# delivered as the thread blocks interruptibly (threadPaused's"] [688 3 "// maybePerformBlockedException; review 189, F5)"] [696 1 "// unblock takes a blocked thread out of what it waits on."] [736 3 "// its throwTo# revoked"] [741 2 "// an interrupted MVar operation leaves no state (review 189, F4)"] [747 1 "// Run runs the program's :Main.main and returns its exit status."] [776 3 "// the program's own C faulted (cprog.go): the process a signal's end, as a C program's"] [799 1 "// reason writes why hsi stopped (HES43 (b)), a word beside its message, on a line of its own: \"hsi-reason: WORD\" (bin/hsi"] [800 1 "// check records it as the result's :reason, a class matches it by its :reasons)."] [803 1 "// fatalReason is the reason of a stop of hsi's own by its message: what it lacks (a primop, a Cmm primcall, a C function,"] [804 1 "// a function pointer, the RTS's API) or a state it cannot go on from (a deadlock), else fatal."] [823 1 "// where describes the current thread's stack for an error message."] [850 1 "// schedule runs threads until until is done (or every thread is)."] [866 6 "// a safe foreign call returning or the first delay expiring, whichever comes first"] [874 6 "// asleep in poll(2) until a descriptor is ready or the first delay expires (awaitEvent)"] [890 5 "// every thread waits for a safe foreign call (the threaded way): until one returns"] [897 4 "// the program's own C threads may still put into an MVar (hs_try_putmvar) or call in: they run first, and"] [898 4 "// while one lives no thread is deadlocked (GHC's: an MVar a C thread can reach by a stable pointer is alive)"] [928 1 "// cIdleNap is the longest nap of cIdle when none of the program's C threads can run now."] [931 1 "// cIdle lets the program's own C threads run while no Haskell thread can (queue 430; the C threads and the machine share"] [932 1 "// crt's baton, one runs at a time): the runnable ones first (crt's Yield), then, when no Haskell thread was woken, a nap of"] [933 1 "// at most d (cIdleNap) in crt's nanosleep, in which the C threads waiting for a time run as it comes. False when the C"] [934 1 "// started no thread or every one it started has ended."] [983 1 "// deadlock is GHC's scheduleDetectDeadlock when no thread can run and none waits for time: a collection (rts.go's"] [984 1 "// gc) resurrects the blocked threads no root reaches; when it resurrects none, the main thread, blocked, gets"] [985 1 "// NonTermination (the non-threaded RTS's last resort). False: nothing to do (hsi stops)."] [997 1 "// runSlice runs t for a time slice, or until it blocks or ends."] [1012 5 "// GHC's threadStackOverflow: StackOverflow raised in the thread, asynchronously"] [1017 5 "// the allocation limit, checked every 256 bounces (GHC: at each nursery block, 4 KiB)"] [1022 39 "// a transaction is not preempted (HES9 (a))"] [1036 3 "// a case continuation run by ret may be compiled code that ran a yield# or a direct call to the budget's end"] [1037 3 "// (HES74 (c): -O1's inline yield#, a forked thread's first chance): the slice ends here too, as it would"] [1038 3 "// after the interpreter's eval of the alternative"] [1049 1 "// shutdown flushes the standard handles (hs_exit's flushStdHandles) and is the exit status."] [1054 3 "// exitScheduler (threaded.go): the other threads deleted, those in foreign calls left"] [1066 1 "// Exit is the program's end requested by shutdownHaskellAndExit: the handles flushed first."] [1080 1 "// CFunctions are the C functions hsi's table has."] [1089 1 "// PrimopNames are the primops hsi implements."] [1098 1 "// Loaded is the number of modules loaded, LoadedBytes their forms' size, Steps the nodes run (by slices)."] [1103 1 "// defaultStackFrames is a thread's frames at most without -K: 2 GiB of frames (GHC's default is 80 % of the host's"] [1104 1 "// memory, which hsi's frames, larger than GHC's words, would reach later than GHC; a bound keeps an endless recursion"] [1105 1 "// from taking the host: the review of HE4d's runs). Loop's 3,000,000-deep chain needs about 10 million."] [1108 1 "// frameBytes is a frame's size, the unit -K's bytes are counted in (GHC counts its stack's words; a frame of hsi's"] [1109 1 "// holds what a few of GHC's words do, so a -K limit is reached at a comparable depth, not the same one)."] [1112 1 "// SetStackLimit sets a thread's stack limit to bytes (+RTS -K)."] [1121 1 "// unwindThunk is a thunk under evaluation an exception unwinds: reverted to unevaluated (asynchronous), or made to raise"] [1122 1 "// again (synchronous); its waiters woken."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[180 71] [224 24] [236 27] [267 18] [276 19] [306 23] [426 26] [459 57] [571 7] [571 15] [601 24] [635 37] [689 35] [755 20] [832 27] [832 44] [990 17] [1018 44] [1132 24]]} (go/file "machine.go" :imports [


